{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117185","id":3367751338,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7Iu86q","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117185","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117185.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117185.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117185","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117185/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117185/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117185/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/34ea182af6f72f4f10d7b23b8520e354f9216d7b","number":117185,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Editor: Fix Bone2D creation to form proper bone chains from selected Node2D hierarchies","user":{"login":"william-saxton","id":79998874,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5OTk4ODc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79998874?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton","html_url":"https://github.com/william-saxton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/william-saxton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"When using \"Make Custom Bone2D(s) from Node(s)\" with a selection that includes\r\nboth a parent and its child Node2D, the resulting Bone2D nodes were previously\r\ninserted at the same level in the scene tree — the parent/child relationship\r\nbetween the original nodes was not reflected in the bone hierarchy at all.\r\n\r\nThis commit fixes that by:\r\n\r\n- Sorting selected nodes by depth (shallowest first) before processing, so a\r\n  parent's bone is always created before its child's bone.\r\n- Tracking a node→bone mapping so that each new Bone2D is reparented under the\r\n  Bone2D created for its Node2D's parent (when that parent was also selected),\r\n  producing a proper bone chain rather than a flat list.\r\n\r\nSeveral correctness issues in the undo/redo logic are also fixed:\r\n\r\n- A `memdelete` was added for the allocated Bone2D when the node has no parent,\r\n  fixing a pre-existing memory leak.\r\n- An early return is added when the selection contains no Node2D instances (e.g.\r\n  only Control nodes), preventing an empty no-op undo action from being pushed\r\n  onto the stack.\r\n- All `_set_owner_for_node_and_children` undo calls are deferred to after the\r\n  structural undo operations (remove/add child) for all nodes have been\r\n  registered. This prevents the recursive ownership walk from descending into\r\n  intermediate Bone2D nodes that are still attached to the tree mid-undo in\r\n  scenes with non-selected nodes between two selected ancestors.\r\n- The original transform is now captured into a local variable before the Bone2D\r\n  is constructed, making the intent of the undo transform restore explicit rather\r\n  than relying on `new_bone->get_transform()` being equal to the captured value.\r\n- Depths are precomputed into a HashMap before sorting, reducing the sort from\r\n  O(n·d·log n) to O(n·d + n·log n) by avoiding repeated ancestor traversals per\r\n  comparison.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"M